    "final_text": "I added `updateQuantity(name, quantity)` to `ShoppingCart` in `src/cart.js`, and the full suite passes (50 tests, 0 failures).\n\n- **Validation:** it checks the quantity before touching any state. Rejected calls (negative, non-integer, non-number, `NaN`, `Infinity`, or an item not in the cart) leave the cart unchanged.\n- **Error types:**\n  - A non-number or `NaN` quantity throws `TypeError`.\n  - A negative or non-integer quantity throws `RangeError`.\n  - An item that isn't in the cart throws a plain `Error`.\n  - All three are `Error`s, so they satisfy your spec. I picked the types to match how `addItem` reports the same problems.\n- **Quantity 0:** it removes the item through `removeItem`. A valid quantity above 0 sets the new quantity directly.\n- **Tests:** new cases in `tests/cart.test.js` cover setting, increasing and decreasing the quantity, the effect on the total, and removal at 0. Each rejection case also checks that the cart is unchanged.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
